- Mid-time onsets (**~4–10 h**) are present across much of the central range (**~4–10 km**), but are less dominant near the farthest distances.
- Late onsets (**~20–32 h**) occur across a broad range of along-strike positions, including near **0 km**, **6–10 km**, and a few farther-strike positions.

### Correlation assessment
- There is **no simple monotonic relationship** between onset time and along-strike position.
- Instead, the panel suggests **spatially discrete clusters** or **episodic activation zones** rather than a single migration front.
